me hi Eleanor Rock has been in Georgia  China and India she's visited more than  50 countries in the last four years to  capture images of female beauty  when I started this project I didn't  have this idea about a global project I  was just aiming for something of  curiosity for myself still doing it  required a leap of faith  no rope quit her job at a TV production  company in Bucharest  at first she lived off her savings then  she started financing her trips through  crowdfunding whether in Myanmar Germany  or Italy the streets and markets are her  workplace no rope approaches women and  photographs them then and there it's  very instinctual process it's a very  maybe some chemistry is going on maybe  some energies are going to be exchanged  between me and that person sometimes  it's just one look and I'm very drawn to  that person in Berlin the Romanian  photographer has been preparing for her  first major solo show she wants  everything to be perfect as these photos  have become part of her life you have to  dedicate yourself completely towards  something that you believe in and  sometimes it just works out sometimes it  doesn't but you have to try otherwise is  like all the women that they approached  many of them they said no I will not be  part of your project I'm afraid and I  didn't give up that's the key in  everything never give up never give up  recently norik also began to collect the  women's stories to ask them about the  challenges in their lives  this woman in Germany beat cancer twice  she fled with her daughters from  war-torn Syria and she works in one of  the most remote regions in the world  these women are all heroes they are  heroes of day-to-day life they are  usually not noticed they go unnoticed  unfortunately but they are heroes for  their families they are heroes for their  friends and I just celebrate them now  their stories and photos have been  published in a book called the Atlas of  beauty it's meant to send a message  everywhere in different forms of course  I think it doesn't have a definition I  think this is our problem as humans  because we try to put it in a box I  think we have to take it out of the box  and understand that beauty has so many  forms  [Music]  soon mihaela no rook will set off again  there are still many countries and more  forms of beauty to explore her project  is far from over  [Music]
 

